+
+# Give each task a unique id
+
+The app needs a stable way to refer to a task that survives a rename.
+
+- `add` returns a task with an `id`: a string no other task of the list has (never reused, even after `remove`).
+- `TaskList.get(id)` returns the task with that id, as a `Result` (`not-found` otherwise).
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+- Ids come from a per-list counter (`task-1`, `task-2`, …): the domain may not use the clock or randomness.
+- When a string is both a task's id and another task's title, the id wins.
